{
 "type": "doc",
 "version": 1,
 "content": [
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "1. What happens now"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The Parts Velocity spreadsheet download prints the \"Last Sale\" column as a piece of text such as "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "54 days",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " instead of the plain number "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "54",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Because the cell is text and not a number, somebody who opens the file in Excel cannot sort by it or use it in a calculation without cleaning the column first."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "2. What should happen instead"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The written description asks for the wording only in the PDF, and a plain number in the spreadsheet."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Parts Velocity specification, version 5, requirement S6-R8: \"Last Sale renders as N days (e.g. 42 days) in the PDF; the CSV renders the raw integer.\""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "3. How to see it"
