  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "4. What was actually in the file"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "{noquote}"
    },
    {
     "type": "hardBreak"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Inventory,BRAKECLEAN,\"Brake & Parts Cleaner\",HD-Fluids,\u2014,\"Staging Heavy Duty - 9919\",512.00,$4.79,$7.69,\"$4,332.11\",\"$1,634.06\",37.7%,416,\"54 days\",618.00"
    },
    {
     "type": "hardBreak"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "{noquote}"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The cell reads "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "\"54 days\"",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " where it should read "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "54",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "5. What was ruled out"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletList",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "It is not the PDF.",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " The PDF correctly prints "
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "54 days",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": ", which is what the written description asks the PDF to do. Only the spreadsheet is wrong."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "It is not one part.",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " Every row in the file carries the same wording."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "listItem",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "It is not an empty value.",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": " A part with no sale at all correctly prints an em dash in both files, so the empty case is handled properly."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "6. How often"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Every time. Four spreadsheet downloads out of four."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "7. Where it was seen"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Reports > Parts Velocity, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " "
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Parts Velocity report specification, version 5, requirement S6-R8, which says: \"Last Sale renders as N days (e.g. 42 days) in the PDF; the CSV renders the raw integer.\" So the words belong in the printable file and a plain number belongs in the spreadsheet."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}